{
  "result": "If I had a magic wand for just one change, I'd make where you're born stop determining whether your potential gets a chance.\n\nEvery child \u2014 no matter their country, family income, or circumstances \u2014 would grow up with the basics secured: enough nutritious food, clean water, basic healthcare, safety, and a good education.\n\nIt's not the flashiest wish. It wouldn't end disagreement, bad decisions, heartbreak, or all suffering. People would still have different values, cultures, ambitions, and arguments about how to live.\n\nBut it would remove desperation as the starting point for billions of lives.\n\nThink of the ripple effects: fewer preventable diseases, fewer conflicts driven by scarcity, more people able to finish school, start businesses, make art, do research, raise healthy families. And how many problem-solvers, teachers, doctors, inventors, and artists are we losing right now simply because someone had to spend their childhood just surviving?\n\nI like that it sets a *floor*, not a ceiling. It doesn't tell anyone who to become \u2014 it just gives everyone a fair shot at becoming who they could be.\n\nWhat would you pick?",
